WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.480
<i>Now then, the 14 remaining Duelists who survived the Park Section</i>

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.610
<i>have broken through and are
 headed to the location of the next battle!</i>

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.070
The light from the blue sky
 overhead the stadium is enveloping them.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.700
They go from the light to the
 pitch darkness of the Underground Section!

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.290
14 of the Coasters survived.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.840
And Yuma's among them, cat!

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.630
Go! Bring it to 'em, Yuma!!

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.180
But Yuma's in 14th place.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.060
He's last place!

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.850
That doesn't meowter!

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.060
This isn't a race, you know.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.490
That's right. The winner will be
 determined through a Duel in the end.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.320
But they can't see anything in such a dark pit.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.570
They have no idea when a a flip side will reveal itself.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.740
No matter what traps await you, cat it to 'em, Yuma!

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.790
<i>Well then, allow me to introduce to you the highlights of the Underground Section!</i>

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.460
<i>Their aim is to decidedly defeat their opponents to determine the strongest.</i>

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>And the battlefields are...</i>

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.260
<i>Magma.</i>

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.700
<i>Space.</i>

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.260
<i>Jungle.</i>

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:20.450
<i>Canyon.</i>

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>Each of the four fields hold special characteristics.</i>

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>Now, lure your opponents into the field that gives you the advantage during your Duels!</i>

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:33.940
<i>Get fired up! Heart Burning!!</i>

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.870
<i>This will be true Hell, unlike before.</i>

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.160
<i>Who will survive...?</i>

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.860
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:56.200
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:13.050
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.850
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.440
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.480
<i>It's too late for us to turn back now</i>

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:34.570
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:40.120
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.920
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.960
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:56.430
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.100
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:08.270
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.360
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.920
Did you hear what Mr. Heartland said, Yuma?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.430
Yeah. Our aim in the Underground Section.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.060
"Number 53: The Fated Rail:
 Try Your Luck on a Trap Card?!"

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.720
We've got to decide which opponent we take down.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.930
Who are you planning to fight against, Yuma?

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.100
Anyone's fine.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.900
I'm gonna do this. I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.650
But there's only four fields.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.070
That means only eight people can Duel there.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.740
Huh? Can't two groups clash at the same time?

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.410
If there's four fields, that means...

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.580
Two groups of four will start off, making eight people in total.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.870
Right! Eight people. It's eight. Huh?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.880
Eh?! Only eight people?!

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.840
Wait... You <i>just</i> realized that?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.340
W-Well...

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.470
That aside, how are we supposed to search for our opponents when it's this dark?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.590
C'mon. There's a map on the monitor.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:10.180
Ah, so you use this to figure out where the others are.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.230
I've taken the lead in first place.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.230
Tron is in second place.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.940
That means Kaito will be third place if this pattern continues.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.650
Tron is...

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.570
I won't let you get away!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.490
This looks interesting!

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.950
I wonder what's waiting up ahead in this darkness!

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.790
My heart's throbbing with excitement!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.170
Tron, I'm the one who's going to fight you.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.580
I'm coming for you.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.630
I'll raise my Life to the utmost maximum, and then I'll...

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.640
IV! I'll catch up with you in no time at all!

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:53.020
I swear to defeat you in this section.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.480
That's it.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.560
That's good. Follow me, Ryouga.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.570
At this rate, I'll lure you right into the Magma Field.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.030
<i>Ryouga... Your deck uses the Water Attribute.</i>

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.620
<i>You have no chance of winning in the scorching hot Magma Field.</i>

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.210
<i>He's the one who kidnapped Haruto before.</i>

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.210
<i>He was looking at the guy during
 the evening festival like he knew him well.</i>

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:25.840
<i>His appearance matches the
 description Yuma gave me back then.</i>

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.800
<i>According to Droite,</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.310
<i>the one manipulating those people who kidnapped Haruto from the background is that guy called Tron.</i>

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.060
<i>V... Tron... Those two are connected somehow.</i>

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.270
<i>I don't know why they kidnapped Haruto...</i>

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.150
<i>...but I'll make you pay for dishonoring my name!</i>

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.110
You're in my way!

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.200
Huh? What the?

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.200
Don't you dare ride in front of me!

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.160
<i>The battles have begun at last!</i>

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.870
<i>Number 13, Burning Toramaru,</i>

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.330
<i>has challenged Number 12, Gauche, to battle!</i>

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.710
I'll kick the crap out of you!

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.630
Go, Wall Creator!

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.760
<i>Shut up! I'm not in the mood
 to play around with some small fry like you!</i>

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.480
I activate the Magic Card, Heroic Call!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:24.110
This card lets me Special Summon
 a Heroic Challenger from my hand!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.150
Come forth, Warhammer!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.490
You're the one who's gonna be kicked about!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.040
Go, Warhammer!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.090
<i>And it ended just like that in an instant kill!</i>

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.140
<i>I expected no less from the former W.D.C. Operation Committee Member, Gauche!</i>

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.180
<i>Not only does he have the looks going for him, he's got exceptional skills!</i>

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.390
Gosh, show Yuma already!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.770
They started a battle over there!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.280
Shit! I gotta hurry and get a battle started!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.570
Whoa, hit the breaks! There's a Trap Point up ahead!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.280
Huh?

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:11.990
Look!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.620
You're kidding...

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.090
Gosh, pay attention properly.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.880
There you are! We got a nice mood going here!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.630
V, I challenge you!

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:37.060
<i>And it's Gauche yet again!
 This time he's challenging V to a fight!</i>

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.810
<i>Show us a fiery battle this time!</i>

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.770
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.150
Hmph. You plan to fight me?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.030
Warhammer! Attack him directly!

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.700
I activate the Magic Card, Radiance of Hell, from my hand.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:02.620
This card negates a Monster's attack 
and sends it back to the hand.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.460
Tch, what a mood killer.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.590
We can't use our full power when you play such cheap little tricks!

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.970
I don't need to use my full power against you.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.850
I activate the Magic Card, Flames of Retribution!

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.100
If inflicts 600 points of damage.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.110
Whoa there! Now <i>Gauche</i> is <i>Burning</i>!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.780
<i>Th-This may be a bit too much for all you good kids at home.</i>

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.120
Oh!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.950
<i>Another battle has started in a separate location!</i>

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.910
<i>It's the Asian Champion, IV!</i>

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.420
Let's get this started now!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.300
Killer Knight, Direct Attack!

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.640
<i>On this side, Number 5, Ryouga, will begin his assault!</i>

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.310
Sick them, Big Jaws!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.850
Big Chew!!

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:11.780
He got me!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:16.490
That's it, Ryouga. Keep following me.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.950
I'll guide you straight into Hell.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.750
IV's so strong! He's so cool!

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.960
Shark's the stronger one!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.960
What gives? IV's the one who's been stronger and cooler all this time!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.840
Shut up! Yuma's obviously the strongest and the coolest!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:35.550
- As if.
 - As if.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:36.880
Cat?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.930
Don't! If you go that way, another-

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.980
Oof...

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.320
Y-You're not looking at all, are you?

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.320
Observation #19...

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.320
Yuma is truly an idiot... after all.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.960
There's a Magic Point up ahead.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.670
If my intuition is correct, it's likely...

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.130
I knew it!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.760
The God of Healing, Dian Keto.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.220
Its effect increases my Life.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.680
7000, huh? It's still not enough.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.890
I need more Life in order to fight him...

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:28.940
What?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:34.820
Tron stopped again... This movement...

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.400
Orbital!

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.700
<i>Yes, Kaito-</i>sama<i>.</i>

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.870
Number two's Coaster, Tron's, is moving suspiciously.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.160
Look into it immediately.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.160
<i>Understood!</i>

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>Tron...</i>

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.960
Another Trap Card.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.310
The Trap Card, Poison of the Butterfly.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:08.600
This is a Trap that will inflict 1000 points of damage unto me.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:14.650
There's Traps laid about all over the place.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.820
I wonder where they're trying to lead me.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.490
Things are getting more interesting.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.790
<i>It's still not enough... More... I need more Life!</i>

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.840
I can't believe you only have 200 points left.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.170
You're in trouble if they decrease any further!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.180
I-It's not like there's anything I can do about it.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:43.890
Losing points during a Duel is one thing,

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.180
but losing them because you fell into a Trap yourself...

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.140
But it couldn't be helped!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.100
Yuma, in front of you!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.730
Eh?!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.400
A-A Trap Point!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.110
Hit the breaks!

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.700
Oh crap!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.490
<i>Again</i>?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.080
The Trap Card, The Paths of Destiny.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.830
You conduct a coin toss

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.210
and if it's heads, your Life Points increase by 2000 points.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.290
If it's tails, you take 2000 points of damage.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.550
2000 points?!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.590
Let's do it!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.260
I'm definitely gonna get heads and increase my points by 2000!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.720
Wait! If you get tails, your Life will be reduced to zero!

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:29.270
I'll recover the Life Points I lost myself!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.270
I figured Yuma would say that.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.610
Here goes! I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:47.620
It's futile, no matter what you do.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.910
Shut up!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.080
Stop wasting time babbling!

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.420
My spirit hasn't fallen yet!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.790
Foolish.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.760
But I've been waiting for this moment.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.930
For the moment my Life fell down to 500!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:09.140
I Summon Heroic Challenger - Double Lance from my hand!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:19.230
This one Monster can be treated as two Xyz Materials!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.820
I Overlay my Level Four Double Lance treated as two Xyz Materials!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.950
I use this Monster twice to build the Overlay Network!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.580
Xyz Summon!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.670
Come forth, Heroic Challenger - Excalibur!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:45.300
Excalibur can't attack unless my Life Points are 500 or lower!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.720
And that time is now!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:52.720
I detach all its Overlay Units in order to double its Attack Power!

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:00.020
Go, Excalibur! Attack V directly!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.730
Single Sword Strike: Sure-Kill Divine Sword!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.110
How laughable.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:10.120
I activate the Trap Card, Those Crawling Into Hell.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:16.790
This card negates the attack of a Monster with 2000 or more Attack Points.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:22.750
And the opposing player takes damage equal to half the Attack Power of that Monster.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:26.880
Wh-What!?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:31.350
To be cut down by the sword of his own comrade...
 I truly pity the fool.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.770
Hold it!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.060
Yuma!?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.480
Use Achachacha Sword Fighter, Yuma!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.900
Right! I Summon Achachacha Sword Fighter from my hand!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.870
Achachacha Sword Fighter springs into action during Effect Damage and negates it,

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.830
inflicting 400 points of damage to the opposing player in the process!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.210
A-Absurd!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.960
<i>My</i> Life...

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.850
<i>Hey, V, are you about to Summon a Monster?</i>

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.060
Tron!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.520
<i>We still need to let him go for now.</i>

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.350
I understand.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.780
Hey, Yuma! Why didn't you chase after him?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.490
You should also hold a grudge against V!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:42.370
More importantly than that for now, you need to focus on recovering your Life first!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.330
Y-You...

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.090
C'mon and follow me!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.250
Hey! Where are you going?

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:55.800
Yuma Tsukumo... Is his aim victory or friendship?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.270
<i>He resembles Kazama quite a bit.</i>

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.020
Kazama Tsukumo...

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:06.480
<i>He valued friendship greatly.
 Perhaps that is what called forth his misfortune.</i>

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:09.070
Here it is!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.450
This is... a Trap Point?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.160
You recovered Life Points with this?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:22.290
Yup! If you get heads in a coin toss, you get your hands on 2000 Life Points.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.500
You're one surprising guy.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.750
You just gotta believe in your luck!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:33.380
But if you fail, your Life Points will be cut down by 2000 instead.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:34.840
You...

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.050
Put all your fighting spirit into that coin toss.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.930
Later!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.650
That bastard...

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:48.110
Oh crap! I fell behind again.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.700
Yuma, a Trap Point!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.550
Yuma!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.440
2950 Attack Points...

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.520
2700...

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.320
4200!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:31.780
Impressive.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:36.280
Little old me up against three top-class Monsters.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.740
This could be trouble.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.760
Three people with one strike...?

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.220
Just how strong <i>is</i> Tron?

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.270
Kaito...

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.730
I can't let Kaito fight with Tron...

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.440
<i>And so they press on!</i>

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:20.280
<i>Out of the 23 Finalists, only 14 survived the Park Section.</i>

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.790
<i>And so far in the Underground Section, six have dropped out.</i>

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:26.910
<i>That leaves us with eight!</i>

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.710
Cat, Yuma!

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:34.250
Yuma finally came out.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:38.930
I was worried he'd be knocked out, but to summarize, he did it!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.510
But the remaining group is incredibly strong!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:46.310
Yuma will be just fine!
 Cat it to 'em with all you've got!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.810
<i>Now, starting now are the one-on-one Duels!</i>

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.230
<i>They are aiming for four of these Duel Fields!</i>

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:56.230
<i>Go into battle, my warriors!</i>

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:59.660
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.080
<i>Now follow after me, Ryouta!</i>

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.330
Since it's come to this, I'll go do
 another coin toss and increase my Life!

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.300
Don't! If you don't get heads next time, you'll only limit yourself!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.760
It's about fighting spirit! Bring it to 'em!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.300
What? A Trap Card?

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.430
That is correct, Kaito-<i>sama</i>.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:27.560
Tron's strange movements

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:31.770
were due to him stopping a series of Trap Cards in his way.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.230
All the set cards had "Butterfly" in their names.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.900
Butterfly cards...?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.790
Droite...

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>Tron is my prey! I won't let anyone else touch him!</i>

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.330
Why are you after Tron?!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.840
I've sworn my allegiance to Mr. Heartland.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:20:00.800
No matter who it is, I will utterly crush anyone getting in his way!

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:05.390
<i>Here it is! This time it's Droite!</i>

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:10.060
<i>She is a former W.D.C. Operation Committee Member. Her Dueling skills are topnotch!</i>

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.480
<i>Advance onward with the revived Gauche!</i>

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:21.070
<i>Droite has indeed sworn her allegiance to me.</i>

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.030
<i>But why would she get in Kaito's way...?</i>

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.450
You're in my way!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.200
I won't let you go! I'm the one who's going to fight against Tron!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.910
Then I will show you no mercy!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:35.130
And I'll return those words to you!

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:39.960
I pay 1000 of my Life Points to activate the Continuous Magic Card, Dance of the Butterfly!

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:46.550
It inflicts 300 points of damage to my opponent for each card with "Butterfly" in its name in my hand!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.640
I reflexively changed my course...

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.440
Live... Kaito!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.780
The Jungle Field is up ahead.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:09.370
If I lure him out into the dense tropical forest, my deck will have the advantage,

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.740
and my chances of winning will increase!

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:16.330
So she's the one who's been trying to lure me into a trap, huh?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:19.840
Fine. I'll take the bait.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.470
If you want to fight me that badly...

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:49.240
Wow... It's like it's a real jungle.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.830
So this is the area you wanted?

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.790
That's right. The Jungle Field...

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.830
The two of us alone will fight here.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.920
Sounds like fun.

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:15.600
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:21.230
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:31.910
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.200
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.500
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:40.210
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:42.840
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:48.010
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:53.390
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:59.020
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:05.480
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:10.950
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:16.240
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:21.830
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:27.090
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:32.590
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:42.980
It's the Duel Carnival Tournament Finals!

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:47.860
Droite and the mysterious masked boy 
duke it out in the Jungle Field!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.150
You're amazing, Droite!

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:53.740
This is a perfect Magic Combo she utilized along with her Field Magic!

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:56.200
The power of love... It's kind lovely.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.620
That Number is...

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.330
Memories? What the heck's that Tron guy up to?

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:02.540
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:07.050
"Tron vs Droite - Allure of the Death Butterfly!
 The Life-Threatening Jungle Field!"

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:08.960
Stop it!!

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:13.050
The Duel Coasters are so much fun!

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:16.050
We don't have the luxury to enjoy the Duel Coasters right now.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:19.180
But I bet they wouldn't hold a candle to Big Sis Akari's motorcycle!

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:19.810
Motorcycle?!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:22.350
Yuma, don't you think it's too much
 for Akari to just take off like that?!

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:24.850
So now you're interested in the motorcycle?!
